 {r}←ReInstallFromDependencies(folders reports parms);i;folder;report;reInstallFlag;reInstallParms;qdmx
⍝ Offers to re-install an install folder from its dependency list, and does so when the user agrees.
⍝ Returns the number of install folders re-installed.\\
⍝ This is offered for a folder that has no later versions on offer but holds at least one package
⍝ the very same version of which is hosted by a Registry other than the one it was installed from;
⍝ see `IsAvailableElsewhere`.\\
⍝ `ReInstallDependencies` copies nothing but `apl-dependencies.txt` into a temporary folder, installs
⍝ everything from scratch there and replaces the install folder only once that has worked. The result
⍝ therefore carries exactly what the dependency list asks for - no package left over from an earlier
⍝ install - and a build list naming the Registries the packages really came from.\\
⍝ Without "update" no version moves anywhere: every pin in the dependency list is honoured as it
⍝ stands, which is what makes this safe to offer while a project is being opened.\\
⍝ A folder carrying one of Tatin's "<<< ... >>>" markers is passed over: such a re-install could only
⍝ fail, because what it would have to fetch is not available.
 r←0
 reInstallParms←⎕SE.Tatin.CreateReInstallParms      ⍝ Both "update" and "major" default to 0: that is the point here
 reInstallParms.quiet←parms.batch
 :For i :In ⍳≢reports
     report←i⊃reports
     :If 0<≢report
     :AndIf ~∨/IsUpdateCandidate report             ⍝ Those are `UpdatePackages`'s business
     :AndIf ~∨/'<'=⊃¨report[;2]
     :AndIf ∨/IsAvailableElsewhere report
         folder←i⊃folders
         :If ~reInstallFlag←2≡parms.checkPackageVersions
             reInstallFlag←1 C.YesOrNo'ReInstallFromDependencies@Re-install <',(AddSlash folder),'> from its dependency list? No version changes'
         :EndIf
         :If reInstallFlag
             1 parms.batch p'Re-installing <',(AddSlash folder),'> from its dependency list ...'
             :Trap 0
                 reInstallParms ⎕SE.Tatin.ReInstallDependencies parms.folder,'/',folder
             :Else
                 qdmx←⎕DMX
                 qdmx.EM Assert~parms.batch
                 1 PrintToSession qdmx.EM
                 :Return
             :EndTrap
             r+←1
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
 :EndFor
⍝Done
